Common HTML Attribute ↔ DOM Property Mappings:


- Before we move to property binding and Why we need it, first let's understand the difference between
    HTML attributes and DOM properties, and how they are mapped.

    HTML Attribute	            DOM Property	            Notes
    id	                        id	                        Same name
    class	                    className	                Different name
    value	                    value	                    Common in forms
    checked	                    checked	                    Checkbox/radio state
    disabled	                disabled	                Boolean property
    selected	                selected	                <option> elements
    readonly	                readOnly	                CamelCase in DOM
    maxlength	                maxLength	                CamelCase
    minlength	                minLength	                CamelCase
    tabindex	                tabIndex	                CamelCase
    colspan	                    colSpan	                    Table cells
    rowspan	                    rowSpan	                    Table cells
    contenteditable	            contentEditable	            CamelCase
    for	                        htmlFor	                    Labels
    readonly	                readOnly	                Input/textarea
    src	                        src	                        Images/scripts
    href	                    href	                    Links
    alt	                        alt	                        Images
    title	                    title	                    Tooltip text
    placeholder	                placeholder	                Inputs
    required	                required	                Boolean
    multiple	                multiple	                Boolean
    hidden	                    hidden	                    Boolean
    open	                    open	                    <details>
    autocomplete	            autocomplete	            Same name
    autofocus	                autofocus	                Same name
    spellcheck	                spellcheck	                Same name
    draggable	                draggable	                Same name
    lang	                    lang	                    Same name
    dir	                        dir	                        Text direction
    type	                    type	                    Input/button type
    name	                    name	                    Form field name
    pattern	                    pattern	                    Regex validation
    min	                        min	                        Numeric/date inputs
    max	                        max	                        Numeric/date inputs
    step	                    step	                    Numeric/date inputs


- ❌“Attribute and property are the same thing.” They often start synchronized, but they are NOT the
    same storage. For example let's create a simple HTML.

        <input value="hello">
    
    Initially:

        input.getAttribute('value') // "hello"
        input.value                 // "hello"
    
    After user types "world":

        input.getAttribute('value') // "hello"
        input.value                 // "world"
    
    🔥In the input example above, the value attribute will always contain 'hello', whereas the value
    property of the DOM node is dynamically modified by the browser, and thus contains whatever the user
    has entered in the text field.
    🔥This is why Angular binds to DOM properties.